[Music]  here's a quick tip from someone we love  hi i'm courtney mack williams i'm the  founder of marymax doggie retreat in new  orleans louisiana and this is gabana i'm  a social worker and i specialize in  overly anxious dogs many facilities  where they're going to abort your dog  offer daycare so have their daycare at  least  two weeks prior to you leaving and  boarding your dog  at least two to three times  that way they're comfortable they know  the staff  it's not a stressful environment for  them that's one of my tips when you're  introducing your pet to a new  environment i would say take them out of  the home starting 10 minutes at a time  to different environments to see how  they would respond what will be good and  comforting for them is  anything that reminds them of home like  their favorite blanket  toy  or  bed even their crate um because  sometimes the crates are their safe spot  that'll help reduce some anxiety if a  thunderstorm is coming and you want to  calm your dog you can use a thunder  jacket but if you don't have a thunder  jacket you can use an old pair of tights  and use their high to their trigger  points right  the nip of the neck  the chest  chest right here  and the back the lower back  you want to swaddle them like a baby  when you tie the tights but you want to  leave the paws  free and the tail free cuddling with  your dog and reading a good book not  only helps to reduce the anxiety of the  dog but as well as the owner  i love animals i'm dr drew little  [Music]

